  "foaf:name": "Achieving Arctic Indigenous Self-Sufficiency",
  "sdo:name": "Achieving Arctic Indigenous Self-Sufficiency",
  "sdo:description": "The Arctic systems are experiencing climate change impacts at a rate 4 times greater than the global average, which present unique challenges to Arctic communities. This Decade Action is an expansion of existing collaborative effort between the Gulf of Maine Research Institute (GMRI) and Innovation South Greenland (ISG), which highlights the climate change impacts to Self-Sufficiency in South Greenland through Indigenous perspectives. The expansion of this work includes building a framework for indigenous co-management in South Greenland fisheries through collaborative work with local stakeholders to build climate resilience in Arctic fisheries. This Action will be built to meet the goals of the Ocean Decade Program: Fisheries Strategies for Changing Oceans and Resilient Ecosystems (FishSCORE). This Decade Action seeks to amplify Indigenous knowledge and give tools to communities and knowledge holders in South Greenland to better address their needs in a research and policy sphere.",
